# 05/10/2026 18:08 — Git Repository Creation

You shouldn't have to create it **if I have a repository-creation action available**. I checked the connected GitHub actions twice because you challenged me.

I can currently:

- create files, branches, commits, issues and PRs;
- modify existing repositories;
- read/search your repositories;
- **but there is no `create repository` action exposed to me.**

So this isn't me handing the work back to you unnecessarily. The connection literally stops one level before repository creation.

**You only need to create the empty repo `enterprise-ai-boundary-research`.** Don't create folders, README, protocol, or anything else.

Once the repo exists, **I do everything else in Git**, including capturing **this turn** in the session audit trail.

